<section class="section install-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span> Install · one command</p>
    <h2 id="install-title">Summon the guild.</h2>
    <p>
      Questmancer is a Herdr plugin, and Herdr installs it for you. It fetches
      the repository, reads the plugin manifest and downloads a checksummed
      binary for your platform. No clone, no Rust toolchain.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p class="install-prerequisite">
    <span class="install-prerequisite-label">Prerequisite</span>
    Install Herdr 0.9.4 or newer with protocol 22 support first:
    <a href="https://herdr.dev/docs/install/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      Herdr install guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </p>
  <div class="terminal" aria-label="Questmancer installation commands">
    <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span>
      <span class="terminal-label">questmancer / install</span>
    </div>
    <pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> herdr plugin install opsydyn/herdr-questmancer
<span class="prompt">$</span> herdr plugin action invoke opsydyn.questmancer.open</code></pre>
  </div>
  <details class="install-source">
    <summary>Using Pi with the guild</summary>
    <p>
      Run <code>herdr integration install pi</code>, then check
      <code>herdr integration status</code>. Start Pi in a Herdr pane, or enter
      <code>/reload</code> in an existing Pi session when it is ready.
      Configure a provider and model supported by your Pi account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Qualified with Herdr 0.9.5, Pi 1.5.2 and integration v9. Working and resting
      reports retain session identity; resting alone does not prove success.
      <a href="https://github.com/opsydyn/herdr-questmancer#use-with-pi">Read the Pi guide</a>.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details class="install-source">
    <summary>New in Questmancer 0.2.0</summary>
    <p>
      The Guild Hall and Delve fit the complete room in compatible terminals,
      with smaller authored sprites and stable seating for larger parties up
      to 64 adventurers. Profiles keep their detailed art. Other panes retain
      responsive half-block scenes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Press <code>b</code> for the Quest Board, then <code>a</code> for Actions.
      Explicitly create or open a local store to author campaigns, quests,
      decisions and artifact registrations. Press <code>w</code> for the War
      Table. Work survives agent sessions; recording an answer or artifact
      does not launch an agent or certify delivery.
      <a href="https://github.com/opsydyn/herdr-questmancer#owned-work-authoring">Read the work guide</a>.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details class="install-source">
    <summary>Building from source</summary>
    <p>
      For working on Questmancer rather than using it. Herdr links a plugin by
      directory, so it needs the manifest and scripts beside the binary.
    </p>
    <div class="terminal" aria-label="Questmancer source build commands">
      <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span>
        <span class="terminal-label">questmancer / source</span>
      </div>
      <pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> git clone https://github.com/opsydyn/herdr-questmancer
<span class="prompt">$</span> cd herdr-questmancer
<span class="prompt">$</span> cargo build --release
<span class="prompt">$</span> herdr plugin link .</code></pre>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
